description: |
  Lists user groups in the current Cortex tenant, returning each group's UUID, display name, assigned role, group type ("Custom" or "AD"), and platform (xdr) tenant identifier. Use this action whenever a group is referenced by display name and you need to resolve it to its canonical "groupId" (UUID) before passing it to another action. Disambiguation rules - when the group is identified by display name:
    - If exactly one group matches, use its "groupId".
    - If multiple groups match (for example "us-soc-analyst" could match "us-soc-analyst-tier1" and "us-soc-analyst-tier2"), do NOT guess. Ask the requester which group they meant (present the candidate display names alongside their groupIds).
    - If zero groups match, do NOT proceed by substituting the raw name string for a real groupId. Inform the requester that no matching group was found and ask for a more specific name.
  This action does NOT return group membership (users, IDP groups, nested groups) or descriptive metadata (description, timestamps, creator).
display: Cortex - List System Groups
isdetailsoverridden: false
locked: false
name: CortexListSystemGroups
outputs:
- description: |
    Unique group identifier (UUID with tenant suffix, e.g. "0de501d3-abab-4d38-a83b-dd3a39af2387_1710886"). Use this value when assigning groups to a case team via CortexUpdateCase.
  disabled: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  name: Core.SystemGroup.groupId
  type: string
  underlyingoutputcontextpath: Core.SystemGroup.groupId
- description: |
    Group display name.
  disabled: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  name: Core.SystemGroup.groupName
  type: string
  underlyingoutputcontextpath: Core.SystemGroup.groupName
- description: |
    Role assigned to this group. May be empty when no role is set.
  disabled: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  name: Core.SystemGroup.roleName
  type: string
  underlyingoutputcontextpath: Core.SystemGroup.roleName
- description: |
    Group type. Possible values: "custom" for custom groups, "ad" for Active Directory groups.
  disabled: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  name: Core.SystemGroup.groupType
  type: string
  underlyingoutputcontextpath: Core.SystemGroup.groupType
- description: |
    Platform tenant (XDR) ID for the group. The value "0" indicates an account-level (cross-tenant) group; any other value is a tenant-scoped group.
  disabled: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  name: Core.SystemGroup.xdrId
  type: string
  underlyingoutputcontextpath: Core.SystemGroup.xdrId
